Aim:
To write a Java program to demonstrate single inheritance.

Algorithm:
1. Create a parent class Animal.
2. Define the eat() method in the parent class.
3. Create a child class Dog using extends.
4. Define the bark() method in the child class.
5. Create an object of Dog.
6. Call both methods and display the output.


Program:
import java.util.Scanner;

class Animal {
    void eat() {
        System.out.println("Animal is eating");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void bark() {
        System.out.println("Dog is barking");
    }
}

public class SingleInheritance {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Dog d = new Dog();
        d.eat();
        d.bark();
    }
}

Output:
Animal is eating
Dog is barking


Result:
Thus, single inheritance was demonstrated successfully.
